Plugins that interact with Lq Explorer at runtime are independent works. This includes plugins that call public APIs, read or write state on the Explorer table, or hook or monkeypatch its functions. Plugin authors keep full copyright and may license their plugins however they choose.

You may copy Lq Explorer source into a plugin under Section 1, but the copied code remains covered by this license wherever it is shipped.

